  "_doc": "Breakers' plate: rust is salvage (console-skins, Vos Syndicate), so the armour is a patchwork of rusts, with about one plate in five still in a maker's colour gone dull (a grey, an olive, a sand); brass (loot and luck) is the one metal kept bright, and there is little of it; the light is verdigris (the spoils kept). Nothing is black: the layer under the plates is a dark rust.",
  "ao_floor": 0.55,
  "accent_share": 0.0,
  "_accent_share": "No whole plate is brass: brass is kept for the two bands (the Breakers' principle 3).",
  "_under": "The layer under the plates, in the seams: a rust a little darker than the plate, never near black, so a seam reads as a fine line, not a drawn one (owner, 2026-11-11).",
  "_machine": "Machinery in the inset panels and the greebles a worn grey against the rust, so the ordered machinery reads apart from the plate (the owner's references, 2026-11-11).",
  "_strip_k": "No glow painted into the maps (owner, 2026-11-11, of the Cross's emitters: \"I don't really like these glowy bits on the cross. They look kinda cheap to me. If you're gonna have glowy bits use baked lighting or shaders\"): a gun's mouth, an emitter and a drive bake as dark metal lenses; the light they cast on the hull round them stays in the baked light map, and the glow itself is a shader on the page (docs/mockups/lib/baked-ship.js lenses). Ship Design Bible T14."
 },
